[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6718503816","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1193#issuecomment-6718503816","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1193","id":6718503816,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkHQ7iA","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T07:00:44Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T07:00:44Z","body":"A bounded provenance finding in the published Worker05 correction is recorded before fixing it: **CATALASE-PROVENANCE-001**. The Catalase proposal says that JCM117 directly supplies the historical C-10 spelling and 60 mg addition. Its declared direct JCM117 capture instead says “Nothing found.” The separate TOGO M109 capture supplies `original_media_id: JCM_M117`, literal `Catalase (Sigma C--10)`, 60 mg and filtration context.\n\nCorrect the attribution to [TOGO M109](https://togomedium.org/medium/M109) and disclose the unsuccessful direct JCM lookup. Preserve the historical catalog spelling, all raw source/history, the distinct verified C9322 product, and the unresolved historical species/C100-equivalence holds. This changes provenance wording, not chemical identity or source transcription. Deduplication read the full current bodies/comments of #1193 and #1201; neither already records this exact finding.\n\nExact finding: `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/integration/final-same-target-reconciliation-v1/finding-catalase-provenance-v1/finding.json`, SHA256 `63159e7a7ce6be15a20f35ae62c42e2e9aabc55b3f319e1c4b688c17a86e2a4f`. No maintained candidate has been applied. The successor requires independent review.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6718503816/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6718699859","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1193#issuecomment-6718699859","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1193","id":6718699859,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkHc5Uw","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T07:23:22Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T07:23:22Z","body":"Reviewed W05 head `43f7cf6e8681fa617b5d6d3529d94d537ca01f0d`, frozen base `e000d66dd26ab053e9b17ce7bf8d3c873c3dde99`. The preserved external review is `20261108T071144Z-worker08-independent-worker05-full188-payload138`, YAML SHA256 `bdde7d4101546e0e43f0752e4587c4d0c3a0fb43f887d82eee2d869edd5c06b0`. All 188 case-decision hashes and all 138 selected payload hashes were independently rebound to the published core; the sealed scientific review remains needs_curation. This comment records bounded follow-up before author correction, not approval or application.\n\nThe final independent review retains eighteen findings. This bounded successor plan keeps their IDs and exact payloads; unresolved family comparisons remain scientific holds rather than being forced into equality or artificial distinctness.\n\n- **W05-CR-F01** — Two HEPES stock owners assert an unsupported substance distinction: Do not infer distinct HEPES stock identities from receiving-medium pH or source numbers. Preserve partial source preparations and all occurrences. Neither equivalence nor selection of a winning source owner is established; coordinate the shared family review before final stable identity choice. Routing: family-findings-triage-v1; #1193 cross-reference.\n- **W05-CR-F02** — Wolfe elixir duplication uses unresolved hydration as proof of distinction: Unknown MnSO4 water count may be one; it is not proof of distinctness from explicit monohydrate. Preserve both complete source recipes and the unresolved bridge. Coordinate C’s W10 mineral/Wolfe family scope; do not mint/merge or pick a winner from richer metadata. Routing: family-findings-triage-v1; #1193 cross-reference.\n- **W05-CR-F03** — Four 95% ethanol owners are distinguished only by receiving recipes: Receiving K1/hemin/menadione preparations do not distinguish the ethanol reagent when excluded from its owner. Preserve all seventeen original occurrences, unknown percent basis/remaining fraction/denaturants, and a conditional comparison. Do not force equality or map unspecified 95% material to an aqueous-v/v ontology term. Routing: family-findings-triage-v1; #1193 cross-reference.\n- **W05-CR-F04** — Generic fatty-acid mixture aliases remain eligible on a recipe-specific stock: Retire or explicitly source-scope the two generic fatty-mixture identity aliases, preserving the JCM266 preparation and raw source history. Exact recipe differences establish that a generic token cannot globally choose JCM266; no new resolver/code is authorized. Routing: 1180.\n- **W05-CR-F05** — Thiamine stock prose generalizes filtration beyond the source: Correct only the new universal filtration attribution: JCM403 specifies the two inputs, while NBRC1321/JCM1125 separately state filtration. Preserve shared formulation, original history and source-specific processing; no forced new owner. Routing: 1193.\n- **W05-CR-F06** — Known wrong thiamine-dihydrate CAS remains despite a feasible bounded removal: Prepare the bounded removal of CAS13465-05-9 from Thiamine-hcl_X_2_H2o.yaml, with exact preimage/history and no invented replacement. Keep CHEBI132751 identity and supported chemistry. Check the coordinator’s latest accepted intake before adding a duplicate proposal. Routing: 268.\n- **W05-CR-F07** — New alias assertions use campaign-only provenance instead of their exact source: Bind thirteen new aliases on eleven owners to their actual recipe/supplier sources; preserve creation-process provenance in history and all older evidence. Correct the NaCOOH caption to actual TOGO M3211 Formate medium. This is assertion traceability, not a new schema rule requiring URLs on every historical synonym. Routing: 1193.\n- **W05-CR-F08** — Inherited active alias conflicts remain on reviewed owners: Separate literal MgSO2/protonation conflicts from generic hydration and concentration scope. Preserve source-proven damaged labels where warranted; do not globally normalize malformed formulas. The nine Mg labels and Nicotinate require individual form evidence; four concentration labels on Riboflavin/Hepes/Ki/Fe_Iii_Citrate require original stock-versus-dose context. Do not infer solvents or complete formulations. Routing: #1229 residual-form aliases and #1230 concentration/preparation aliases.\n- **W05-MAT-001** — Generic soy owner still asserts branded product and alternative aliases: Apply the already sourced Phytone scope decision and its three exact Soy_Peptone alias withdrawals, then separately address retained Soytone/Bacto Soytone product scope against authentic history/manufacturer evidence. Reconcile W08/W10 competing owner deltas without mergers, count redistribution or automatic shared-ID memberships. Routing: 1212.\n- **W05-MAT-002** — Fish-sperm DNA owner retains generic and conflicting tissue aliases: Retain the fish-sperm/SERVA source identity and reject the unsupported generic-DNA or conflicting-thymus exact-identity aliases with raw provenance preserved. Do not infer species, length/counterion, reverse the herring tombstone or resurrect the false absent-formula/class premise of #322. Routing: fish-sperm-generic-aliases.\n- **W05-MAT-003** — Known truncated concentration token remains on generic Peptone: Retain Peptone (0.01 % as rejected provenance, without reconstructing a preparation, percentage basis or supplier. Preserve Peptones and source/organism holds. This narrow alias correction does not resolve the separate eighteen existing component-reference and current cross-shard Peptone identity dependencies. Routing: 1193; preserve historical 208/218 context.\n- **W05-MAT-004** — Bacto owner retains a fish-product alias despite the mammalian product boundary: Extend the product-alias repair to Fish peptone (Fluka), which conflicts with Bacto’s evidenced mammalian product scope. Preserve the exact text/source/history; do not infer a Fluka product, move counts or decide every other generic meat/mixture alias. Routing: 1176.\n- **W05-MAT-005** — Metadata tokens remain in the Catalase and soy synonym channels: Actual native probes show all three Properties strings already nonresolving in both MIM and Claw76c1. Optional provenance-preserving REJECTED_LABEL classification is not a live resolver fix, acceptance blocker or reason to change filters. Preserve the original peer observation rather than rewriting it. Routing: 1193 qualification only.\n- **W05-MAT-006** — Optional typed sucrose component link is available: Optional exact sucrose component link may improve the partial 20% w/v stock; §6 permits named UNMAPPED components. No required global component-grounding rule, solvent guess, concentration reinterpretation or extra role approval follows. Routing: 1193 qualification only.\n- **W05-MAT-007** — Catalase provenance claims a direct JCM source although the captured endpoint is empty: Already filed exact source-attribution defect: substantive TOGO M109 preserves JCM117 lineage, while retrieved direct JCM117 says Nothing found. Check the coordinator’s exact reconciled Catalase v2 before duplicating the fix. Keep C--10/C9322/C100 identities and human-NCIT exclusion separate. Routing: 1193 comment6718503816; coordinator Catalase v2.\n- **W05-MEDIA-F01** — Active Marine Broth mapping evidence retains the superseded agar-equivalence premise: Correct the retained active mapping-evidence claim that commercial broth differs from agar only by gelling agent. Preserve original assertion historically and bind the actual manufacturer broth formula; do not undo the supported component correction or approve release. Routing: 1208.\n- **W05-MEDIA-F02** — EMJH quantitative curation is deferred by a false basis conflict: Transcribe the five explicit approximate basal amounts with the manufacturer’s per-liter basis and performance-adjustment footnote. 2.3/0.9≈2.55556 g/L agrees with the approximate 2.555 g/L sum, so that arithmetic alone is not a scientific blocker. Do not infer final enriched-medium concentrations, exact lot composition, phosphate hydrate or thiamine salt. Routing: 1193.\n- **W05-MEDIA-F03** — Cooked-meat evidence claim is attached to an unrelated environmental-noise PDF: Withdraw the positive USDA1998/chapter14 attribution from the active evidence index and dependent evidence links. Preserve the exact unrelated EPA noise PDF and retrieval metadata as an unsuccessful/mismatched retrieval. An actually retrieved relevant source may replace the claim, but the two independently supported component-reference withdrawals need not be reversed. Routing: 1193; linked owner obligations748.\n\nThe current exact native probe qualifies MAT-005: the two Catalase Properties strings and one Soy_Peptone Properties string are already filtered in both maintained MIM and pinned Claw76c1. No current exported-alias defect is inferred. MAT-006 is also optional; named ungrounded components are permitted. These qualifications supplement the immutable review rather than rewriting its findings.\n\nAll new mapping-evidence assertions must also satisfy #1226's human-only enum distinction, preserving genuinely historical human evidence and the separate component-evidence enum semantics. Exact science does not become approved through a type correction. Preserve the existing Peptone identity/component-reference coupling (eighteen historical dependents plus current cross-shard proposals), and the Phytone, Bacto and other shared-owner reconciliation decisions; do not silently retarget component owners.\n\nPrepare an immutable report-only successor accounting for all 188 original source cases and every one of the 138 selected original proposals. Add feasible bounded proposals (such as the false-CAS removal) or state the real remaining fact; do not hide authorized work behind an unrelated hold. Additional or superseded proposals may change the final count. Preserve the prior core files, exact captures, review lineage, failures and source-specific limitations. Revalidate every final payload through existing strict schema, guarded serialization and full-overlay partonomy, then obtain independent whole-payload/source re-review. No corpus application, new gate/code, approval widening or shared export rebuild is part of this author task.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6718699859/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6718748704","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1193#issuecomment-6718748704","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1193","id":6718748704,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkHf4IA","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T07:29:06Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T07:29:06Z","body":"Independent follow-up to the preserved W06 review `20261108T071757Z-w06-ten-unions-independent-metadata-v2` (authoritative YAML SHA256 `01a7f358f637ce22e8db311ca290c92e010fad757120f1ae43e89265b1742e32`). I verified all 670 manifest-listed proof files and independently matched the ten reviewed payloads to the active 37-candidate set. These are unapplied candidates, not owner or release approvals. Original reviews, source captures and histories remain immutable.\n\n**W06-TU-004 — a bounded BSA source-context correction.** The current reconciled `Bovine_Serum_Albumin.yaml` candidate SHA256 `d9c58b2297f6aef28850dac72e708f3a0df3eac949693ba8d2edd1c1de26f9bc` preserves a new W05 note at `supplied_form[5].notes`: “manufacturer/catalog and final ADC/OADC volume not established.” This entry's case70, `CM_NAME:8ba1df295abb60b7fb8cd7e12f80b861e3d2e7634dd64e3bfb7e88df0db0fd08`, is [TOGO M194 / JCM201 BSK medium](https://togomedium.org/medium/M194), not ADC/OADC.\n\nThe complete source capture SHA256 `84717c209dda5e9fc18a4ee5b1456ee655f243d31013b41b0d118ff17d03bdb9` explicitly lists Bovine albumin, Fraction V,50g. It has mixed volume-bearing ingredients and final rabbit-serum supplementation, without a justified exact final volume for a protein-concentration calculation. Replace only the irrelevant ADC/OADC context with truthful BSK context and the unresolved final preparation volume. Preserve literal Fraction V, unknown supplier/catalogue,50g source amount, recipe membership and source history. Do not convert this amount to50g/L.\n\nThis is distinct from #1222's JCM220/MediaDive3888 occurrence quantity. Preserve its independently reviewed WITHHOLD correction and all other full-companion claims. The BSK wording repair neither re-approves that quantity nor establishes inherited A7030 processing/purity claims. Record the narrow correction in a new immutable reconciled candidate and obtain independent review; no owner, role or release approval is granted here.\n\n<!-- mim-fingerprints:bsa-case70-bsk-context-note -->\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6718748704/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6719161955","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1193#issuecomment-6719161955","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1193","id":6719161955,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkH5GYw","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T08:16:17Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T08:16:17Z","body":"Record five additional findings from Worker05's independent review of its unpublished correction draft. These are `W05-FINAL-SKEPTIC-CHEM-001` through `005`. Original findings and failed/intermediate drafts remain evidence; this comment does not claim that every diagnostic report correction was made after GitHub filing. No maintained ingredient change has been applied.\n\n1. **001, bottom-layer explanation:** the primary-conclusions draft incorrectly contrasts FeS with zero-valent iron. JCM629 explicitly reuses JCM628 with artificial saltwater replacing Modified Wolfe mineral solution; both bottom layers retain the FeS preparation and agarose. Correct the report explanation while preserving the already-correct selected payloads. Root verified the complete captured JCM628/629 texts.\n2. **002, MKP attribution:** the primary-conclusions draft calls MKP a JCM salt preparation. The complete MediaDive record identifies DSMZ medium1895 and MKP solution6635, a multicomponent medium base including CMRL1066, Neopeptone, HEPES and glucose. Correct report attribution and scope; the selected payload already cites MediaDive1895.\n3. **003, thiamine-HCl monohydrate completeness:** six NBRC recipes1550/1443/1444/1445/1447/1507 explicitly print the one-water label. Root rehashed and read all six primary captures. Missing CAS, fixed molecular structure or chloride/protonation detail prevents exact molecular grounding; it does not alone rule out a bounded source-defined material under MAPPING_SEMANTICS§3. Reassess one shared nominal monohydrate candidate after ignored-inclusive owner/proposal checks, retaining all six occurrences and both source cases. Do not infer CAS, formula, chloride stoichiometry, supplier, anhydrous/dihydrate equivalence, an exact parent relation, or a separate owner per source number. If an actual owner-boundary ambiguity prevents that representation, document it precisely. The exact successor still requires independent review; this finding is not an identity approval.\n4. **004, reviewer prose count:** the DSMZ95% ethanol grouping has twelve applicable occurrence IDs: eleven flat occurrences plus DSMZ212a. The exact occurrence list was already correct; change the review's “eleven” wording while retaining its predecessor. This supplies no new percentage basis or product-equivalence decision.\n5. **005, reviewer grade wording:** the Tris hydrochloride payload stores `NARROW_MATCH`, and the pinned native projection emits `skos:broadMatch` plus CAS and local identity rows. Two review sentences incorrectly say the stored grade is `BROAD_MATCH`. Correct those sentences; retain the already-correct payload and projection. This is a report correction within the separately filed#1238 decision, not a grade-rule change.\n\nThe bounded source-completion task remains under this issue. Retain each finding's real timestamps, original severity and before/after evidence; do not recast earlier internal report revisions as post-filing repairs. Independently review final selected bytes, complete case/proposal retention and every unchanged scientific hold before publication. Private root readback and complete original findings are in `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/preflight/w05-review-followups-triage-v1/`. There is no new role, whole-owner or supported-export approval.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6719161955/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6719577911","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1193#issuecomment-6719577911","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1193","id":6719577911,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkISfNw","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T09:02:35Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T09:02:35Z","body":"Independent bounded completion finding: `COMBINED37-COMPONENT-GROUNDING-001`.\n\nThe frozen, unapplied 37-candidate packet preserves a blanket UNMAPPED disposition for all 16 Marine Broth parts and all nine Difco RCM parts. The source evidence supports at least the three exact references below. Uncertain hydrate forms and undefined peptones do not justify withholding these literal salt identities.\n\n| Exact candidate | Component index (zero-based) | Printed nominal input | Supported existing owner |\n|---|---:|---|---|\n| TARGET-012, Marine_Broth_2216.yaml, SHA256 `34ce518a98ba30ee826ddd083687df477ab796a28f494b015e5bea82841e4dcf` | 3 | Sodium chloride, 19.45 g/L at standard reconstitution | Nacl.yaml, CHEBI:26710 |\n| Same | 7 | Potassium chloride, 0.55 g/L at standard reconstitution | Kcl.yaml, CHEBI:32588 |\n| TARGET-032, Reinforced_Clostridial_Medium.yaml, SHA256 `431d24db8ff93084d5cb2260cd016b9d1a466561d618c68a6e2dd4e78c7f2c28` | 4 | Sodium chloride, 5 g/L at standard reconstitution | Nacl.yaml, CHEBI:26710 |\n\nPrimary sources: the [Marine manufacturer table](https://cdn.media.interlabdist.com.br/uploads/2021/01/Marine-2216-Agar-e-Broth.pdf), SHA256 `de2504598b1133074ba2239c045958e9a6564dc1b2a2d8f13ab4bac99233199f`, and [Difco RCM table](https://cdn.media.interlabdist.com.br/uploads/2021/01/Reinforced-Clostridial-Medium.pdf), SHA256 `e11b1ff246e72286261ac3d7117711bde8b59669a8ea365fa9dd75d298cb2864`. Exact manufacturer ingredient names agree with the current [sodium chloride ontology definition](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:26710) and [potassium chloride ontology definition](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:32588), independently read alongside the complete current MIM owners. No unprinted hydrate, stereochemistry, commercial subproduct or dissolved ion is inferred.\n\nKeep the literal component names, nominal amounts/units and manufacturer adjustment footnotes. Add only the supported MIM_CATALOG references and claim-specific evidence/history. Independently assess the remaining constituents one by one; leave genuinely unresolved form/product claims UNMAPPED. This finding does not authorize blanket mapping of the other salts, peptone or every yeast/extract preparation. Existing #1208 broth-versus-agar, #1224 supplier partition, #1176 peptone, source, role and release obligations remain separate.\n\nIndependent counterfactual: adding exactly these three references in memory passes the native closed schema and full 2,957-record overlay partonomy, with no corpus writes. This verifies that the existing native contract accepts the precise supported links; it does not approve the complete owners or publication. Exact before/after cells and owner hashes are in `component-grounding-probe.json` under `preflight/combined37-v3-independent-v1`.\n\nDeduplication: fresh complete #1208/#1224 bodies and comments already cover formulation correction and supplier scope, but not these three missing exact references. This is a coherent addition to the campaign completion work on #1193, cross-linked to #1208/#1224; it need not create another owner/parent-identity issue. Rebind final published origins and independently review the corrected combined bytes before application. The active 37 packet has a declared historical source cutoff, and later worker source corrections also need incorporation.\n\n<!-- mim-fingerprints:combined37-component-grounding-001 -->\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6719577911/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6719578158","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1193#issuecomment-6719578158","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1193","id":6719578158,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkISgLg","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T09:02:36Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T09:02:36Z","body":"Independent review reported `W07-W05-MAT-PARENT-001`, an additional exact-target scope of the parent-grounding mechanism in #1202. The current W05 Soy peptone and generic Peptone proposals retain only FALLBACK_REGISTRY self-mappings despite source-supported protein-hydrolysate families. This is inherited incompleteness, not a regression introduced by the final provenance corrections.\n\nExact current payloads remain unchanged at published `76bca688b4f55e8bdf791079df8d4156cded6c4c`: `W05-FINAL-MAT-032` Soy_Peptone SHA256 `e37e3230f9b4489e715cda9c1785f30ea97305d1d6264045bea75b92312bf236`, and `W05-FINAL-MAT-039` Peptone SHA256 `61590bc2de78646c368ed1fb21c2c29bbc041d9f248e8a712c578376e776996d`. The manufacturer guide defines the protein-digest family without requiring a supplier or mammalian origin. Bound FoodOn evidence identifies FOODON:03315720 vegetable protein, hydrolyzed and FOODON:03315306 protein hydrolyzates. Inspect their complete ontology scope/annotations and source applicability before choosing the closest supported parent and asymmetric predicate under MAPPING_SEMANTICS section3; a label alone is not sufficient.\n\nComplete the supported nonidentity family relation while preserving each distinct local identity and native registry obligation. Do not restore the unsupported mammalian identity, infer a branded Soytone/Phytone product, assert an anatomical has-part relation, merge owners or approve roles/exports. Preserve source/form/organism holds, old objects/history and exact source-case lineage. Use a guarded successor with native projected rows and independent complete-byte review; if a proposed parent is unsupported after full inspection, document the precise reason rather than guessing.\n\nIndependent finding: W07 `.temp/w05-final-correction-independent-v1/review/materials/findings.json`, SHA256 `2f9624cecfe18322f75b75c7ba2247a6fbe68aabc40cdb93c66e1e175baa603d`. Root froze the reported index at `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/preflight/w05-final-completion-findings-publication-v1/review-finding-index-at-read.json` SHA256 `9587223471020191df48220150bf0c875e7b011a3dcd1c2de0731fd9a67e6e7e` and checked the actual current payloads and ontology captures. Manufacturer PDF SHA256 `963de777a42013795b1dd6f3fd2820ef3010d659fa501d5991d18cebd0243fa6`; FoodOn captures `aa063e8b88177611aba640828e84d3982b1b3b1c65b11647d89c9efbf6274c25` and `c6264c268afeadcb47631173e6a803cbf9a0b7a8c08fda990df55ee260680f28`. Reported before dependent fixes; no source application or approval occurred.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6719578158/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6719578394","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1193#issuecomment-6719578394","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1193","id":6719578394,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkIShGg","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T09:02:38Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T09:02:38Z","body":"Independent finding `W07-W05-MEDIA-REPORT-001` adds four exact active caption targets to the existing media-report provenance work. Root verified that the same strings remain in the selected decisions at published `76bca688b4f55e8bdf791079df8d4156cded6c4c`; the frozen case identities and scientific payloads are correct.\n\n| Zero-based case | Unsupported unqualified caption | Actual ingredient source | Bound solution/recipe context |\n|---|---|---|---|\n|130|MediaDive1315|mediadive.ingredient:559|mediadive.solution:1201; DSMZ542|\n|135|MediaDive2528|mediadive.ingredient:1467|mediadive.solution:3366; DSMZ1619|\n|144|MediaDive1137|mediadive.ingredient:748|mediadive.solution:1635; DSMZ804|\n|158|MediaDive581|mediadive.ingredient:2095|mediadive.solution:651 and5601; DSMZ339/339a|\n\nAffected field: `final_correction_reassessment.assessment`, plus its selected derived media-report copy. Correct to the demonstrated fully qualified identifiers, or supply an authentic exact source for an alternative namespace. Do not equate ingredient, solution and medium numbers. Preserve original text in immutable predecessor evidence and bind the successor metadata explicitly; no payload, quantity, ingredient identity, frozen occurrence or source capture change is requested.\n\nExact case IDs, field strings, object hashes and primary captures are in W07 `.temp/w05-final-correction-independent-v1/review/media/findings.json`, SHA256 `8ce56172402fc9bb87d457b148d559cbed402906649e3857124e91e7ed93c95b`. Root's frozen reported index is SHA256 `9587223471020191df48220150bf0c875e7b011a3dcd1c2de0731fd9a67e6e7e` at `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/preflight/w05-final-completion-findings-publication-v1/review-finding-index-at-read.json`. This extends #1193 before correction; all other independent findings and scientific/role/release holds remain.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6719578394/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6719660443","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1193#issuecomment-6719660443","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1193","id":6719660443,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkIXhmw","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T09:11:19Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T09:11:19Z","body":"Independent exact-instance followup to the Soy/Peptone grounding comment on #1193. No record change has been applied.\n\nFor the generic Soy peptone proposal, evaluate **MICRO:0000181 (soy peptone)** before selecting a local identity with a broader FOODON anchor. MAPPING_SEMANTICS §3 gives a supported specific ontology identity precedence over a registry fallback. The actual nonobsolete MicrO term describes mixed enzymatic soybean-flour digest; its definition-source annotation cites the BD Bionutrients Technical Manual's general discussion of enzymatic soy-flour digests. The OLS parent response for Phytone contains this generic term. Being a parent of Phytone does not make Phytone or a named Soytone product identical to generic Soy peptone.\n\nThe exact archived OLS response is `workers/w03/worktree/.temp/combined-products-independent-v1/products/supplemental/micro1795-parents.body` (campaign-relative), SHA-256 `367675d648bbf157b20727e908eee325cfc1363c601c82a9b9e7f32f81084287`. Its retrieval metadata records the official OLS endpoint `https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/api/ontologies/micro/terms/http%253A%252F%252Fpurl.obolibrary.org%252Fobo%252FMICRO_0001795/parents`, accessed 2026-11-08T06:53:39.724860+00:00. The reviewer read the actual term object and its definition-source annotation, not only its label.\n\nThe source-side generic context is the successful MediaDive ingredient 75 response (`https://mediadive.dsmz.de/rest/ingredient/75`), SHA-256 `96988f7bda2d96e92ead61edd385a8f50523aaae8f0b0f48e5f1e6f37e341ecd`, preserved in the frozen combined packet's `origin-evidence-v1/captures/` directory. It names Soy peptone and soybean/soymeal synonyms, reports CAS 91079-46-8 and supplies no branded-product identity. The separately failed `/compound/75` request is not evidence for absence.\n\nScope exclusions are essential: do not import the term's erroneous **Hordeum vulgare** parenthesis, branded Bacto/Soytone or papaic synonyms as exact owner aliases, or the annotated 12% ash / 0.2% NaCl as universal composition. Generic enzymatic digest support does not establish a specific enzyme, supplier, lot, peptic-process alias, or equality with Phytone/Soytone siblings. Preserve the existing five branded/alternative alias withdrawals, all occurrence-allocation and incoming-reference obligations, and all physical-form, role and export holds. A current immutable exact-source successor still needs independent review and native dependency checks.\n\nThis is a bounded direct-generic-term recommendation for Soy, not a choice of parent for Peptone or Polypeptone. Their actual ontology options and definitions must be assessed independently; no FOODON target is prescribed solely from a label or the SIREN flavoring annotation.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6719660443/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6719869465","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1193#issuecomment-6719869465","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1193","id":6719869465,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkIkSGQ","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T09:34:21Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T09:34:21Z","body":"Conditional dependency audit for the proposed Soy peptone identity correction: source evidence for MICRO:0000181 remains subject to the actual final scientific review. This audit does not approve that term or a release.\n\nComplete parsed inventories of both current isolated maintained trees (2,956 records and 502 components each), all 1,006 exact committed selected proposal payloads (2,618 component slots), and the 37 composed candidate owners found no incoming component_id reference to FOODON:03315720, kgmicrobe.ingredient:soy_peptone, MICRO:0000181 or MIM:Soy_Peptone. Ignored files were included in the discovery search. Thus no additional component-consumer assignment beyond the already filed generic-Peptone dependency work is demonstrated.\n\nThere are separate real continuity obligations before any identifier migration:\n\n- FOODON:03315720 is shared by four active owner records and the rejected Bacto_Soytone tombstone. Its 828 membership rows / 1,079 occurrences are shared-ID associations, not a proved Soy-only partition. Do not globally redirect them.\n- The tombstone representative pointer cannot be silently redirected or left asserted as a uniquely identified Soy owner. Record an explicit reviewed disposition; any record correction needs its own authentic proposal and beforeimage.\n- The exact duplicate-baseline membership changes when Soy and independently reviewed Phytone depart. Refresh only the specifically reviewed family after final owner selection; no gate or threshold relaxation.\n- Native source-label routing, membership/count reconciliation, canonical rows and derived/unified products need review against the final owner bytes. Zero incoming partonomy edges does not establish source membership.\n\nFrozen audit: preflight/soy-identifier-dependency-preflight-v1/HANDOFF.json SHA256 8152e1060340ad7a934030be1e5a8c881ce3794dba4f1a8d9fe94eb683c76c47; MANIFEST SHA256 74f9ed0b9161fe5fdae9b61e2637b13af1f670c35caa4394f3c00bad82e1a114, all 59 members rehashed by the coordinator. The local committed selector cutoff includes W05 0bac12ca and W08 4a404256; the later no-core W08 replay is not inferred as new science. No maintained or source files changed in this audit.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6719869465/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]